{
  "manufacturer": "DEIF",
  "manufacturer_slug": "deif",
  "model": "SGC 420 Mk II Single Genset Controller",
  "model_slug": "sgc-420-mk-ii",
  "short_model": "SGC 420 Mk II",
  "aliases": [
    "SGC 420 MkII",
    "SGC 420 Mk2"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Generator controller",
  "applies_to": "SGC 420 Mk II software R19.0 (Modbus tables revision C).",
  "summary": "The SGC 420 Mk II is DEIF's second-generation single genset controller with RS-485 Modbus RTU. Values can be read as holding registers (function 03) or input registers (function 04) at the same addresses. This map covers the 16-bit generator, mains, load and engine readings, run-time counters, the packed I/O and genset-status words and the mode-change command.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": null,
    "baud": null,
    "parity": null,
    "data_bits": null,
    "stop_bits": null,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "0-based",
    "note": "The tables print plain register numbers starting at 0 (register 0 is the protocol revision / mode command), with no 4xxxx prefix, so the printed number is the request address. The same numbers work with function 03 and function 04."
  },
  "default_word_order": null,
  "firmware": "R19.0",
  "source": {
    "title": "SGC 420 Mk II Modbus tables",
    "doc_number": "4189341402 rev. C",
    "revision_date": null,
    "url": "https://deif-cdn-umbraco.azureedge.net/media/bxrpobcf/sgc-420-mk-ii-modbus-tables-4189341402-uk.xlsx",
    "pages": "Spreadsheet sheet 'Holding & Read (03;04;16)'"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Scaling values in the table (0.1, 0.01) are used as multipliers here even though the column header reads 10^-x; the values only make sense as multipliers, and the first-generation SGC tables use the same numbers as plain multipliers.",
    "Left out: the energy counters 39-50 (listed as FLOAT32 CDAB but also with a 0.1 scaling, which leaves it unclear whether the float is already in kWh) and the run-hours overflow word at 60. Percentage load (30) is left out because its unit is printed as kW.",
    "Left out: the alarm-state words 72-88 (four 4-bit alarm states per word, values 0 disabled, 1 not active, 2 warning, 3 shutdown, 4 electrical trip, 5 notification). They share the bit-numbering caveat below and are not split here.",
    "Word 89 packs inputs P (table bit 1) up to A (bit 16); word 90 packs outputs G (bit 10) up to A (bit 16). Word 91 packs, from table bit 1 up: common notification, common warning, common electric trip, common shutdown, gen available, fail to start, stopped with fault, stopped normally, DG running, load on DG, load on mains, operation mode (bits 12-14: 100 manual, 101 auto, 110 scheduler), mains healthy, SGC mode (bit 16). The table numbers bits 1-16 without saying whether bit 1 is the least significant bit, so the words are listed whole.",
    "Also not listed: the packed time-stamp bytes, the CPCB IV+, EGR and DTC blocks and the J1939 values passed through from the engine ECU.",
    "See the user manual 4189341360 for wiring and the RS485 menu: https://deif-cdn-umbraco.azureedge.net/media/uvtnn0df/sgc-420-mk-ii-user-manual-4189341360-uk.pdf",
    "Also not listed: auxiliary inputs S1-S4 (65-68) and the site battery values (69-71), which have no unit printed."
  ],
